{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20","id":1482019,"title":"Holy Strike in C20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-26T12:52:31-07:00","id":1482019,"title":"Holy Strike in C20","content":"So, is it me or is this power really buffed?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: The Realm used determines the target of the cantrip \u2014 who or what is destroyed. <b>The activation roll for this cantrip doubles an attack roll</b>. This cantrip has a maximum striking range of (changeling\u2019s Willpower x 10) yards/meters, and inflicts dice of lethal damage equal to the changeling\u2019s (Willpower + Glamour + additional successes on the activation roll). </div> </div> </div>So, besides the damage from Willpower + Glamour, it doubles the attack roll? Did I understand it right? For instance, if the PC attacks with a sword using dexterity 4 + melee 4, would he roll 16 dice in the attack roll? I don't quite remember the exact phrasing of the original, but besides being in a different Art now, it seems buffed (although without the alternative to heal instead of causing damage etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:33:30-07:00","id":1482023,"title":"","content":"People usually say Changeling and co. in Dark Ages Fae are so powerful, but there isn't anything even remotely close to this in Dark Ages Fae lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:52:09-07:00","id":1482025,"title":"","content":"I'm 99.9% positive that's a typo (I'm not sure if it got corrected or addressed at some point; esp. given the issues with the book's developer) and it's supposed to be, &quot;doubles as an attack roll.&quot; That is, your activation roll is your &quot;to hit roll,&quot; rather than having to roll to activate, roll to hit, and then roll damage if you pull off both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:52:19-07:00","id":1482026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20#post1482019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is it me or is this power really buffed?<br /> <br /> <br /> So, besides the damage from Willpower + Glamour, it doubles the attack roll? Did I understand it right? For instance, if the PC attacks with a sword using dexterity 4 + melee 4, would he roll 16 dice in the attack roll? I don't quite remember the exact phrasing of the original, but besides being in a different Art now, it seems buffed (although without the alternative to heal instead of causing damage etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it is strong, the sentence is &quot;...doubles AS an attack roll...&quot; So you roll your Art + realm activation roll and that is your attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:54:10-07:00","id":1482027,"title":"","content":"Ninja'd. But yeah. I pulled out the printed book and the AS is present. You might still have your pre erata version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T14:02:58-07:00","id":1482029,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see, so it's as I suspected. Otherwise, it would put to shame every other power possessed by Fae in the Dark Ages (although it is still more potent than most, by far as it is). I don't know if I'm happy or sad knowing this is a typo lol, Changelings are usually so under powered when compared to other &quot;night folks&quot; that it would be cool if they had an op power like this hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:18:55-07:00","id":1482329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1482029#post1482029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I'm happy or sad knowing this is a typo lol, Changelings are usually so under powered when compared to other &quot;night folks&quot; that it would be cool if they had an op power like this hahaha</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? My impression is quite the opposite, while most people don't look at them much they're extremely powerful, specially their magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T22:15:43-07:00","id":1483014,"title":"","content":"What if the changeling decides to make Holy Strike as fire attack? Fire causes aggravated damage (especially deadly against vampires), what could limit the changeling from using that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T22:23:33-07:00","id":1483016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483014#post1483014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the changeling decides to make Holy Strike as fire attack? Fire causes aggravated damage (especially deadly against vampires), what could limit the changeling from using that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. The Changeling can do that freely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T22:37:36-07:00","id":1483018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483016#post1483016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. The Changeling can do that freely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But then the damage would be aggravated (and basically a one-hit-kill against, at least, 90% of the vampires in the world lol). That's quite fearsome for a level 4 power hahaha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T11:34:37-07:00","id":1483057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483018#post1483018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then the damage would be aggravated (and basically a one-hit-kill against, at least, 90% of the vampires in the world lol). That's quite fearsome for a level 4 power hahaha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling magic is the most directly potent in the WoD, the only limiting factor being access to Glamour and their disposition for Bunks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Try using Wayfare's Hopscotch on an opponent to crash them on their allies and put them where you want. Go ahead, make some calculations at 4 or 5 successes and tell me what you think. It's just a level 1 power, you can bring the difficulty as low as 3 with some effort and use it as basis for an Unleashing to add your Nightmare to the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 06-04-2022, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:35:49-07:00","id":1483075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483018#post1483018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then the damage would be aggravated (and basically a one-hit-kill against, at least, 90% of the vampires in the world lol). That's quite fearsome for a level 4 power hahaha.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really even scratching the surface of all the weird things changelings can pull off. One of the Most Famous examples is using the Wayfare 1 power: Hopscotch with Scene 5 and Prop 4 Realms to make Buildings jump onto whatever they're looking at.<br /> <br /> Also remember that a changeling can use extra glamour to substitute for missing levels in realms, so a starting changeling with Wayfare 1 can do this if they got a hold of a lot of glamour/dross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T19:36:23-07:00","id":1483095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483075#post1483075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really even scratching the surface of all the weird things changelings can pull off. One of the Most Famous examples is using the Wayfare 1 power: Hopscotch with Scene 5 and Prop 4 Realms to make Buildings jump onto whatever they're looking at.<br /> <br /> Also remember that a changeling can use extra glamour to substitute for missing levels in realms, so a starting changeling with Wayfare 1 can do this if they got a hold of a lot of glamour/dross.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was so common and blatant that in C20 Hopscotch <b><u>specifically</u></b> states that Scene + Prop with it allows for affecting multiple objects, but <b>not buildings</b>, albeit also saying that affecting buildings is possible with an <b><i>Unleashing</i></b> of Wayfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T21:33:44-07:00","id":1483102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483095#post1483095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was so common and blatant that in C20 Hopscotch <b><u>specifically</u></b> states that Scene + Prop with it allows for affecting multiple objects, but <b>not buildings</b>, albeit also saying that affecting buildings is possible with an <b><i>Unleashing</i></b> of Wayfare.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure that move was banned By Name in core as far back as second edition, but the players straight up ignored it because it was The Iconic &quot;YOU HAVE PISSED OFF THE FAE!&quot; move(typically reserved for Mages who thought they were the most powerful supernatural to ever exist and were trying to rub the &quot;fairies&quot; noses in it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-05-2022, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T02:29:10-07:00","id":1483114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483075#post1483075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really even scratching the surface of all the weird things changelings can pull off. One of the Most Famous examples is using the Wayfare 1 power: Hopscotch with Scene 5 and Prop 4 Realms to make Buildings jump onto whatever they're looking at.<br /> <br /> Also remember that a changeling can use extra glamour to substitute for missing levels in realms, so a starting changeling with Wayfare 1 can do this if they got a hold of a lot of glamour/dross.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol, but this is way gonzo and a ST can simply say &quot;no&quot;, it's very different from a clear system that states you can cause &quot;30&quot; dice of fire damage with an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T07:10:30-07:00","id":1483123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483114#post1483114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol, but this is way gonzo and a ST can simply say &quot;no&quot;, it's very different from a clear system that states you can cause &quot;30&quot; dice of fire damage with an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing though. The changelings Are gonzo, that's part of the point. Walking their pet attack-house is just one example of how the changelings can do crazy.<br /> <br /> CtD is basically built around being an allegory for playing pretend and how as we grow older we lose touch with our inner child. Part of that is just the Shear unadulterated crazyness that kids come up with in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T07:17:25-07:00","id":1483124,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why CtD has the Mists; it would be nearly impossible to conceal their existence otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T07:59:33-07:00","id":1483126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483102#post1483102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that move was banned By Name in core as far back as second edition, but the players straight up ignored it because it was The Iconic &quot;YOU HAVE PISSED OFF THE FAE!&quot; move(typically reserved for Mages who thought they were the most powerful supernatural to ever exist and were trying to rub the &quot;fairies&quot; noses in it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember this in 2nd ed, but I admittedly didn't read it in a long time. Either way, it is explicitly possible with <b><i>Unleashing</i></b>, so it is officially approved now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483114#post1483114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol, but this is way gonzo and a ST can simply say &quot;no&quot;, it's very different from a clear system that states you can cause &quot;30&quot; dice of fire damage with an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually both RAW and RAI, so by saying &quot;no&quot; you're houseruling. As I said, C20 specifically states this feat as a possible <b><i>Unleashing</i></b>.<br /> <br /> So the point is that Changeling is actually meant to be gonzo. It is about dreams and creativity, about childish play made real, and about emotion and wonder over realism. Changelings are powerful and bold, with little regard for safety.<br /> <br /> When you need limits for them, you use <b>Banality</b> and <b>Bedlam</b>. By tying such feat to <i><b>Unleashing</b></i> the game is also making clear that it risks plunging the character one more step in the direction of madness, and Mad Changelings are even more banned from reality than Marauders. They're sad wretches trapped within their nightmarish freeholds and the clutches of their own minds, powerful but ultimately pitiful little things incapable of meaningful interactions or meaningful impact, the <b>Lost Ones</b>.<br /> <br /> It is a long road, so it isn't something the PCs need to avoid at all costs, but it is still far from hard to travel if they don't take care. And the only known and relatively reliable cure for this is grounding yourself in the Autumn, avoiding magic and gonzo solutions to your problems, avoiding freeholds and preferably avoiding large Changeling gatherings, or avoiding Changelings at all if they're not going to help. And while the idea is to find the creative outlets and fulfillment within a mundane life, it still means a higher risk of <b>Banality</b>, which is made worse by the fact that <b>Banality </b>and <b>Bedlam</b> aren't mutually exclusive, and a failed treatment may well become a contest between apathy and psychosis to see which takes the final toll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T11:23:04-07:00","id":1483495,"title":"","content":"God, this thread has reminded me how much I love this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:04:27-07:00","id":1483525,"title":"","content":"Still, discounting all the gonzo things I don't like, the fact is that I still don't think a building would have the potential to cause 30 aggravated to vampires lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:51:19-07:00","id":1483533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482019-holy-strike-in-c20?p=1483525#post1483525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, discounting all the gonzo things I don't like, the fact is that I still don't think a building would have the potential to cause 30 aggravated to vampires lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that I totally agree. As weird as it seems, I don't think the actual weight of a building should account for damage as it is big enough for things to get a lot more complicated. It would cause Lethal at most, and not such a huge amount. If you keep their integrity you're basically doing a certain level of Cartoon Physics and the victim is entitled a good chance at surviving, if not then the damage should be more similar to a collapsing building, which is something chaotic but a lot of people can survive at first.<br /> <br /> It would bury them, though. Which wouldn't be a life-threatening thing for a Vampire. Or would put them in the basement, which is also an option. Adding another aspect of the game, that Changeling magic is empowered by the Dreaming, and it is a Realm of Stories, I would most probably make the damage quite survivable and let the victim in the basement.<br /> <br /> That's another thing to always keep in mind, you can and should, as an ST, define the results of any supernatural effect related to the Dreaming by your notion of what's the best story to be told, because the Dreaming actively does that instead of just letting Changelings have fine control of the outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}